{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.genus_filtration_ideal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_filtration_ideal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_filtration_ideal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_filtration_ideal","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L49-L109","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\nThe genus of the moduli surface is not assumed --- it is\n**determined by the Iwahori--Hecke algebra**.  The QOU axioms force\n$g = 4$ through a completeness condition on the irreducible\nrepresentations of $H_2(q) \\oplus H_3(q)$, and the\ngenus-filtration ideal $\\mathfrak{I}_4 = (u^5)$ is the\nalgebraic obstruction that kills $T_{2,p}$ for all primes\n$p \\geq 11$.\n\n## Part 0: the genus is determined by the algebra\n\n**Proposition (Genus from Hecke completeness).**\n*Let $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ be a QOU with\n$G = \\mathrm{SU}_q(2)$.  The braiding on $V_1^{\\otimes n}$\ngives the Iwahori--Hecke algebra $H_n(q)$.  The relevant strand\ncounts are $n = 2$ and $n = 3$:*\n\n- *$H_2(q)$ has $2$ irreducible representations\n  (partitions of $2$: $(2)$ trivial, $(1,1)$ sign).*\n- *$H_3(q)$ has $3$ irreducible representations\n  (partitions of $3$: $(3)$, $(1,1,1)$, $(2,1)$).*\n- *Total: $5$ irreps.*\n\n*At genus $g$, the embeddable torus knots $T_{r,s}$ with\n$(r-1)(s-1) \\leq 2g$ and $\\gcd(r,s) = 1$ are the ones whose\nJones polynomials can be evaluated on $\\Sigma_g$.  Completeness\n([cohomological embedding](#prop:cohomological-embedding))\nrequires that these evaluations **span all $5$ irrep\ncharacters**: the evaluation matrix\n$M_{ij} = \\chi_{\\lambda_j}(\\sigma_i)$ must have rank $5$.*\n\n*The strand counts $m \\geq 4$ contribute no new knots: at genus\n$g$, the constraint $(m-1)(s-1) \\leq 2g$ with $m \\geq 4$ and\n$m < s$, $\\gcd(m,s) = 1$, gives $s \\leq 2g/(m-1) + 1$, which\nfor $m = 4$ yields $T_{4,3} = T_{3,4}$ (already counted) and\nfor $m \\geq 5$ yields no valid $(m, s)$ pairs with $m < s$.\nTherefore $H_2(q) \\oplus H_3(q)$ is the complete Hecke\nalgebra of the QOU.*\n\n**The genus scan.**\n\n| $g$ | Embeddable torus knots | Count | Rank of $M$ | Complete? |\n|:---:|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| $2$ | $T_{2,3}$, $T_{2,5}$ | $2$ | $\\leq 2$ | No |\n| $3$ | $T_{2,3}$, $T_{2,5}$, $T_{2,7}$, $T_{3,4}$ | $4$ | $\\leq 4$ | **No** |\n| $4$ | $T_{2,3}$, $T_{2,5}$, $T_{2,7}$, $T_{2,9}$, $T_{3,4}$, $T_{3,5}$ | $6$ | $5$ | **\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The proposition is **named** below as a `def … : Prop` (pattern C):\n    the Hecke evaluation matrix and filtration ideal are opaque\n    categorical inputs, so the four-part claim is recorded as the\n    conditional conjecture over the context rather than discharged by a\n    fake projection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:genus-filtration-ideal","label":"prop:genus-filtration-ideal","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-filtration-ideal.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.kills_T_2p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.kills_T_2p","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Predicate: torus knot `T_{2, p}` is killed by the ideal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.ideal_exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.ideal_exponent","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Generator exponent of the ideal `I_g = (u^k_g)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.genus","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The Riemann-surface genus chosen by the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.EvalMatrixRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.EvalMatrixRank","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The representation-evaluation matrix `M_{ij} = χ_{λ_j}(σ_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.ObstructionClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.ObstructionClass","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Cohomology / obstruction class type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.Link","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.Link","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Topological link / torus-knot type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.PartitionIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.PartitionIdx","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Partition / Young-diagram indexing for irreps of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.Braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.Braid","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Braid representative type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusFiltrationIdealContext","kind":"class","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/genus_filtration_ideal.lean#L27-L47","doc":"Abstract context (inputs) for the `genus_filtration_ideal` claim —\nthe categorical braid / partition / link / obstruction data, the\nevaluation-matrix rank, the genus, the ideal exponent, and the\nabstract `kills_T_2p` predicate.  No field asserts a conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}